## Lessons for Developing Traders

TimeToFire's profile offers several actionable insights for traders refining their own Polymarket strategies. The first lesson concerns the psychology of win rates. Many traders, conditioned by traditional financial markets or gambling contexts, fixate on winning percentage as the primary measure of skill. Prediction markets reward a different calculus. The question is not how often you win but whether your wins sufficiently exceed your losses in magnitude. A trader comfortable with a 20% win rate can take positions that risk-averse competitors avoid, positions where the potential upside dramatically exceeds the probability-weighted expected value implied by current prices. The second lesson involves volume as a strategic tool. High-volume traders gain experience faster, develop intuition for market microstructure more quickly, and position themselves to capture value when major events unfold. The third lesson is about commitment to a defined strategy. TimeToFire's consistent high-volume approach across 26 markets suggests disciplined adherence to a methodology rather than reactive, emotion-driven trading. Whether or not this specific approach suits every trader, the consistency itself is instructive.

