TimeToFire's presence in the top 40 by verified profit underscores a fundamental truth about prediction markets: there is no single path to success. Some traders win through patient, selective positioning with high win rates and modest position sizes. Others, like TimeToFire, succeed through volume, accepting frequent small losses as the price of being positioned when major moves occur. The $564,838 in cumulative profit represents real value extracted from markets through a methodology that many would dismiss based on its 20.88% win rate alone. For observers and competitors alike, this profile serves as a reminder to evaluate trading approaches by their outcomes rather than their surface-level metrics. The leaderboard does not care about win rate elegance or theoretical soundness. It measures dollars gained and lost, and by that measure, TimeToFire has earned a place among Polymarket's proven performers.

